<template>
    <heading>Select/Create Project Dialog</heading>
    <keywords>
        <li>dialog</li>
        <li>project selection</li>
        <li>project creation</li>
        <li>modal</li>
    </keywords>
    <section data-lp5-kind="explanation">
        <p>This article defines the Select/Create Project dialog markup. Its code bundle name matches the dialog template's DOM <code>id</code>, so the parent dialog-template container can insert it with a code reference. The dialog-specific behavior belongs to the <code>SelectCreateProject</code> operation, selected by the logical <code>dialogName</code> on a <code>ModalDialog</code> command.</p>
        <p>When mounted, the dialog script body is compiled with <code>LP5.util.scriptToFunction</code>. The wrapper supplies an <code>elementByID</code> map, so each button has a unique id and the script can bind directly to it. Clicking a button dispatches a command named by its <code>data-action</code>.</p>
    </section>
    <section data-lp5-kind="code">
        <name>SelectCreateProject</name>
        <code><![CDATA[
<template id="SelectCreateProject">
    <style>
        .SelectCreateProject {
            text-align: center;
        }

        .SelectCreateProject h2 {
            margin: 0 0 1rem;
            font-size: 1.25rem;
        }

        .SelectCreateProject .dialog-buttons {
            display: flex;
            justify-content: center;
            gap: 1rem;
        }
    </style>
    <dialog class="SelectCreateProject"
            aria-labelledby="SelectCreateProject-title">
        <h2 id="SelectCreateProject-title">Select or Create a Project</h2>
        <div class="dialog-buttons">
            <button id="SelectCreateProject-Select" type="button" autofocus data-action="Select">Select</button>
            <button id="SelectCreateProject-Create" type="button" data-action="Create">Create</button>
        </div>
        <p data-name="selectionError" role="alert"></p>
        <script>
            for (const action of ["Select", "Create"]) {
                const button = elementByID[`SelectCreateProject-${action}`];
                button.addEventListener("click", () => {
                    window.LP5.controller.dispatch({
                        name: button.dataset.action
                    });
                });
            }
        </script>
    </dialog>
</template>
]]></code>
    </section>
</template>
